        <mxCell id="c117" value="&lt;i&gt;Report view, page Ex B.2, viewed as the Sales Manager in the role Cost Center Managers. The table lists the first 19 of the 120 rows of AccessEmployees, in the order of its first column, which a table has without a sort of its own; the scroll bar shows how long the list is. Outlined: the two terminated employees in view, whose dates show, as do the other eleven below. No rule filters a table that no relationship reaches, so the Sales Manager sees every row, while Employee itself shows only the 8 of the Sales cost center. The text box is the model answer&#x27;s note, cut to a few lines of each paragraph.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="578" width="860" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
